Butt welding procedure of hot melt welding machine

Hot-melt butt welding must use a hot-melt butt welding machine to heat the end face of the PE pipe, so that the surface is quickly melted and bonded, under a certain pressure, and after cooling, the two are welded. Polyethylene pipes of different sizes can be welded by this method, preferably a polyethylene pipe with a nominal diameter of not less than 90 mm. Hot-melt butt welding is economical, even when the joint is pulled or compressed, it can produce higher strength than the pipe itself.

1) Pipe components can be clamped, the pipeline can be flattened by the bracket, and the concentricity can be adjusted and controlled, and the out-of-roundness of the pipeline can be checked and corrected by the fixture, and a certain welding distance can be reserved in advance;

2) Milling the welding surface, milling a certain thickness, ensuring that the welding end surface is smooth and parallel, ensuring that the gap of the butting end surface is not more than 0.3mm, and the amount of wrong side is not more than 10% of the wall thickness of the welding place. If re-clamping, re-milling is required;

3) Measure and check the drag pressure, as long as the welding is performed, the measurement and recording work must be carried out;

4) Heating is a relatively important link. First, the heating plate must be placed, and the welding pressure (P1) is adjusted = dragging pressure (P dragging) + welding specified pressure (P2). If the height of the circumferential curling protrusion at the welding place around the heating plate exceeds a certain value, reduce the pressure to P drag;

5) Switch the docking, pull out the heating plate within a certain time, quickly fit the welding surface, and steadily increase the pressure to P1 to avoid high-pressure collisions;

6) Disassemble the pipeline components, cool for a period of time, and wait for the pressure to drop to zero to disassemble the pipeline components.

Hot melt butt welding process control

The control of the hot melt welding process is carried out for the hot melt welding step, rather than the quality judgment of the final weld joint quality. Among them, several influencing factors are very important, including temperature, time and pressure. Because polyethylene pipe hot-melt welding is

 electrofusion welding is the absence of a flash that violates the standard pipe permeability. The application of electrofusion technology is especially relevant in a limited space when it is impossible to use large-sized welding equipment. Operation sequence of electrofusion welding is:

  1. A specialized tool is used to cut  polyethylene pipes to the desired length.
  2. The electric coupling and the welded pipe sections are thoroughly cleaned of debris, dust and persistent contaminants;
  3. To control the immersion depth in the coupling, marks are applied to the pipes;
  4. At the far ends of the pipes, plugs are installed that eliminate the risk of heat loss;
  5. The electric coupling is connected by wires to the welding device;
  6. The welding process begins after pressing the start button;
  7. The welding machine automatically shuts off when the process is completed;
  8. The welded joint is suitable for use after cooling and complete hardening.

During cooling, the immobility of the welded parts is observed to form a durable welded joint. The thickness of the high-quality weld bead is from a third to half the thickness of the pipe walls. The maximum permissible axial displacement of the welded pipe segments is not more than 10% of the wall thickness. The weld bead should cover the previously applied mark.

